1
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:54,750
Attack Force Z is a war, action film directed by Tim Burstall.

2
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:43,500
Sent to rescue survivors from the site of a plane crash in the South Pacific during WWII, Captain Kelly and his elite squad
of Australian commandos must keep tabs on a defecting Japanese official who could hold the secret to peace.

3
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:32,250
Captain Kelly, played by Mel Gibson.

4
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:21,000
Lieutenant Veitch, played by John Phillip Law.

5
00:29:03,750 --> 00:29:09,750
Sergeant Costello, played by Sam Neill.

6
00:34:52,500 --> 00:34:58,500
Able Seaman A.D. 'Sparrer' Bird, played by Chris Haywood.

7
00:40:41,250 --> 00:40:47,250
Chien Hua, played by Sylvia Chang.

8
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Lin Chan-Lang, played by Ko Chun-Hsiung.

9
00:52:18,750 --> 00:52:24,750
Attack Force Z (alternatively titled The Z Men) is a 1982 war film directed by Tim Burstall,
and starring John Phillip Law, Mel Gibson, Sam Neill, and Koo Chuan Hsiung.

10
00:58:07,500 --> 00:58:13,500
It dramatizes the exploits of Z Special Unit, also known as Z Force, a
joint Australian, British and New Zealand commando unit.

11
01:03:56,250 --> 01:04:02,250
Its main brief was to conduct reconnaissance and sabotage missions throughout
Imperial Japanese-occupied Southeast Asia during the Second World War.

12
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:51,000
The film is noted for starring Mel Gibson and Sam Neill, who were relatively unknown
in the US at the time but who went on to become international stars.

13
01:15:33,750 --> 01:15:39,750
It was an international co-production between Australia and
Taiwan, and was filmed on-location in Taiwan.

14
01:21:22,500 --> 01:21:28,500
It was screened at the Cannes Film Festival on 18 May 1981.

15
01:27:11,250 --> 01:27:17,250
The film explores themes of mission, submarine,
world war ii, airplane crash, commando.
